			"path": "src/main/ffmpeg.ts-simstep-36d955c0-cf85-4369-a68e-66bcbd4af8e1",
			"fileName": "ffmpeg.ts",
			"wiki": "In the main process, `runFfmpegConcat` spawns the `ffmpeg` executable as a child process. It pipes the `concatTxt` string to the process's standard input, which ffmpeg reads to know which files to concatenate. It also attaches a progress handler to provide feedback to the UI.",
			"cellName": "Execute FFmpeg Process - ffmpeg.ts:L135-145",
			"cellId": "d8c3f6fb-df84-4939-9cff-0ec29342cce5",
			"visible": true,
			"startLine": 135,
			"endLine": 145,
			"parentCellId": "23b5178b-602e-4c79-9363-db6d14a91c86",
			"parentPath": "src/main/ffmpeg.ts",
			"simSteps": [
				{
					"simulationKey": "Merge and concatenate multiple media files",
					"simStepId": "36d955c0-cf85-4369-a68e-66bcbd4af8e1"
				}
			]
		},
