			"fileName": "ffmpeg.ts",
			"wiki": "In the main process, the 'captureFrames' function (or a similar single-frame equivalent) receives the data. It constructs the precise command-line arguments for the ffmpeg executable, including input file, output path template, quality options, and filters. It then spawns the ffmpeg process to create the image file.",
