		"Merge and concatenate multiple media files": {
			"name": "Merge and concatenate multiple media files",
			"simSteps": [
				{
					"simStepId": "76642823-e06f-4c3b-9891-cc0f0bc02447",
					"diagramNodeId": "09c9b42c-d62a-42c0-9508-d23e22b6b8f7",
					"simStepLabel": "Configure Concatenation",
					"simStepDescription": "The user interacts with the ConcatDialog to select multiple media files, arrange their order, and choose output options. This dialog is shown when multiple files are loaded and the merge action is triggered.",
					"isEdge": 0,
					"sourceCodeMapping": {
						"filePath": "src/renderer/src/components/ConcatDialog.tsx",
						"startLine": "38",
						"endLine": "42",
						"relevantVariables": [
							"ConcatDialog",
							"paths",
							"onConcat"
						]
					},
					"inputDataExample": "{\"isShown\": true, \"paths\": [\"/path/to/video1.mp4\", \"/path/to/video2.mp4\"]}",
					"outputDataExample": "{\"sortedPaths\": [{\"path\":\"/path/to/video1.mp4\"}, {\"path\":\"/path/to/video2.mp4\"}], \"outFileName\": \"merged-output\", \"fileFormat\": \"mp4\", \"includeAllStreams\": true}"
				},
				{
					"simStepId": "aa2ae219-ffd2-44d2-a046-40fe71795b9c",
					"diagramNodeId": "0186f8b3-f7c5-4e4a-8924-849b9fbd9bb8",
					"simStepLabel": "Transmit Concatenation Request",
					"simStepDescription": "When the user clicks the 'Merge!' button, the onConcat prop is called, sending the configured file paths and options from the ConcatDialog component to the main App component.",
					"isEdge": 1,
					"sourceCodeMapping": {
						"filePath": "src/renderer/src/App.tsx",
						"startLine": "2825",
						"endLine": "2825",
						"relevantVariables": [
							"ConcatDialog",
							"onConcat",
							"userConcatFiles"
						]
					},
					"inputDataExample": "{\"paths\": [\"/path/to/video1.mp4\", \"/path/to/video2.mp4\"], \"includeAllStreams\": true, \"streams\": [], \"outFileName\": \"merged-output.mp4\", \"fileFormat\": \"mp4\", \"clearBatchFilesAfterConcat\": true}",
					"outputDataExample": "{\"paths\": [\"/path/to/video1.mp4\", \"/path/to/video2.mp4\"], \"includeAllStreams\": true, \"streams\": [], \"outFileName\": \"merged-output.mp4\", \"fileFormat\": \"mp4\", \"clearBatchFilesAfterConcat\": true}"
				},
				{
					"simStepId": "2b0f9f2c-100b-4d91-88ec-4b8b1ac2af0a",
					"diagramNodeId": "cad1a6a7-423e-46ec-ace6-76725d1e110c",
					"simStepLabel": "Handle Concatenation in App",
					"simStepDescription": "The `userConcatFiles` function in the main App component receives the request. It sets the application's state to 'working', determines the output path, and then invokes the `concatFiles` function from the `useFfmpegOperations` hook to perform the core logic.",
					"isEdge": 0,
					"sourceCodeMapping": {
						"filePath": "src/renderer/src/App.tsx",
						"startLine": "954",
						"endLine": "956",
						"relevantVariables": [
							"userConcatFiles",
							"concatFiles",
							"paths",
							"outPath"
						]
					},
					"inputDataExample": "{\"paths\": [\"/path/to/video1.mp4\", \"/path/to/video2.mp4\"], \"includeAllStreams\": true, \"streams\": [], \"outFileName\": \"merged-output.mp4\", \"fileFormat\": \"mp4\", \"clearBatchFilesAfterConcat\": true}",
					"outputDataExample": "{\"paths\": [\"/path/to/video1.mp4\", \"/path/to/video2.mp4\"], \"outPath\": \"/path/to/output/merged-output.mp4\", \"outDir\": \"/path/to/output\", \"outFormat\": \"mp4\", \"metadataFromPath\": \"/path/to/video1.mp4\"}"
				},
				{
					"simStepId": "328d3bc7-f86b-4f1f-aa5b-397cc218bc0f",
					"diagramNodeId": "0b8931ae-4545-4f35-bff3-c6162f6a07fb",
					"simStepLabel": "Invoke FFmpeg Operation",
					"simStepDescription": "The parameters required for concatenation are passed from the `userConcatFiles` function in App.tsx to the `concatFiles` function inside the `useFfmpegOperations` custom hook.",
					"isEdge": 1,
					"sourceCodeMapping": {
						"filePath": "src/renderer/src/App.tsx",
						"startLine": "954",
						"endLine": "956",
						"relevantVariables": [
							"concatFiles"
						]
					},
					"inputDataExample": "{\"paths\": [\"/path/to/video1.mp4\", \"/path/to/video2.mp4\"], \"outPath\": \"/path/to/output/merged-output.mp4\", \"outDir\": \"/path/to/output\", \"outFormat\": \"mp4\", \"metadataFromPath\": \"/path/to/video1.mp4\", \"includeAllStreams\": true, \"streams\": [], \"ffmpegExperimental\": false, \"preserveMovData\": true, \"movFastStart\": true, \"preserveMetadataOnMerge\": true, \"chapters\": []}",
					"outputDataExample": "{\"paths\": [\"/path/to/video1.mp4\", \"/path/to/video2.mp4\"], \"outPath\": \"/path/to/output/merged-output.mp4\", \"outDir\": \"/path/to/output\", \"outFormat\": \"mp4\", \"metadataFromPath\": \"/path/to/video1.mp4\", \"includeAllStreams\": true, \"streams\": [], \"ffmpegExperimental\": false, \"preserveMovData\": true, \"movFastStart\": true, \"preserveMetadataOnMerge\": true, \"chapters\": []}"
				},
				{
					"simStepId": "bf39d6ba-5ec6-4d8a-823f-b23a2d4e3ae1",
					"diagramNodeId": "70da5496-b0ae-4694-a3ef-a7b72d6b100b",
					"simStepLabel": "Prepare FFmpeg Command",
					"simStepDescription": "The `concatFiles` function constructs the necessary ffmpeg arguments. It generates a text string (`concatTxt`) that lists all the input files in the format required by ffmpeg's `concat` demuxer. This string will be piped to the ffmpeg process.",
					"isEdge": 0,
					"sourceCodeMapping": {
						"filePath": "src/renderer/src/hooks/useFfmpegOperations.ts",
						"startLine": "111",
						"endLine": "229",
						"relevantVariables": [
							"concatFiles",
							"ffmpegArgs",
							"concatTxt",
							"runFfmpegConcat"
						]
					},
					"inputDataExample": "{\"paths\": [\"/path/to/video1.mp4\", \"/path/to/video2.mp4\"], \"outPath\": \"/path/to/output/merged-output.mp4\"}",
					"outputDataExample": "{\"ffmpegArgs\": [\"-f\", \"concat\", \"-safe\", \"0\", \"-i\", \"-\", \"-c\", \"copy\", \"/path/to/output/merged-output.mp4\"], \"concatTxt\": \"file '/path/to/video1.mp4'\\nfile '/path/to/video2.mp4'\"}"
				},
				{
					"simStepId": "cad68aa3-fc9d-4488-afe2-43523061942a",
					"diagramNodeId": "5e112657-7093-422f-99dc-40e08322c517",
					"simStepLabel": "Send Command to Main Process",
					"simStepDescription": "The `runFfmpegConcat` function is called. This function is exposed from the main process via Electron's IPC mechanism, sending the prepared ffmpeg arguments and the concat text to the main process for safe execution outside the renderer's sandbox.",
					"isEdge": 1,
					"sourceCodeMapping": {
						"filePath": "src/renderer/src/ffmpeg.ts",
						"startLine": "17",
						"endLine": "17",
						"relevantVariables": [
							"runFfmpegConcat"
						]
					},
					"inputDataExample": "{\"ffmpegArgs\": [\"-f\", \"concat\", \"-safe\", \"0\", \"-i\", \"-\", \"-c\", \"copy\", \"/path/to/output/merged-output.mp4\"], \"concatTxt\": \"file '/path/to/video1.mp4'\\nfile '/path/to/video2.mp4'\", \"totalDuration\": 360}",
					"outputDataExample": "{\"ffmpegArgs\": [\"-f\", \"concat\", \"-safe\", \"0\", \"-i\", \"-\", \"-c\", \"copy\", \"/path/to/output/merged-output.mp4\"], \"concatTxt\": \"file '/path/to/video1.mp4'\\nfile '/path/to/video2.mp4'\", \"totalDuration\": 360}"
				},
				{
					"simStepId": "36d955c0-cf85-4369-a68e-66bcbd4af8e1",
					"diagramNodeId": "d8c3f6fb-df84-4939-9cff-0ec29342cce5",
					"simStepLabel": "Execute FFmpeg Process",
					"simStepDescription": "In the main process, `runFfmpegConcat` spawns the `ffmpeg` executable as a child process. It pipes the `concatTxt` string to the process's standard input, which ffmpeg reads to know which files to concatenate. It also attaches a progress handler to provide feedback to the UI.",
					"isEdge": 0,
					"sourceCodeMapping": {
						"filePath": "src/main/ffmpeg.ts",
						"startLine": "135",
						"endLine": "145",
						"relevantVariables": [
							"runFfmpegConcat",
							"runFfmpegProcess",
							"process",
							"stringToStream",
							"concatTxt"
						]
					},
					"inputDataExample": "{\"ffmpegArgs\": [\"-f\", \"concat\", \"-safe\", \"0\", \"-i\", \"-\", \"-c\", \"copy\", \"/path/to/output/merged-output.mp4\"], \"concatTxt\": \"file '/path/to/video1.mp4'\\nfile '/path/to/video2.mp4'\"}",
					"outputDataExample": "{\"pid\": 12345, \"command\": \"ffmpeg -f concat -safe 0 -i - -c copy /path/to/output/merged-output.mp4\"}"
				},
				{
					"simStepId": "f57067fd-2230-4040-9cd3-a33046e56f17",
					"diagramNodeId": "ddfd7506-8251-470c-aee0-57550402eafa",
					"simStepLabel": "Return Execution Result",
					"simStepDescription": "After the ffmpeg child process completes, a result object containing stdout, stderr, and the exit code is returned asynchronously from the main process back to the renderer process.",
					"isEdge": 1,
					"sourceCodeMapping": {
