					"diagramNodeId": "045068fd-d4a9-48b1-a694-665dbd4b09a4",
					"simStepLabel": "Determine Stream Handling for New Container",
					"simStepDescription": "The export logic calls helper functions to determine how each stream should be handled. Based on the target `outFormat`, it decides whether a stream can be directly copied (`-c copy`) or needs to be re-encoded to a compatible codec (e.g., converting mov_text subtitles to srt for a Matroska container).",
					"isEdge": 0,
					"sourceCodeMapping": {
						"filePath": "src/renderer/src/util/streams.ts",
						"startLine": "122",
						"endLine": "170",
						"relevantVariables": [
							"getPerStreamFlags",
							"isMov",
							"outFormat",
							"addCodecArgs"
						]
					},
					"inputDataExample": "{\"stream\": {\"codec_type\": \"subtitle\", \"codec_name\": \"mov_text\"}, \"outFormat\": \"matroska\"}",
					"outputDataExample": "{\"codecArgs\": [\"-c:0\", \"srt\"]}"
				},
				{
					"simStepId": "f01cf11f-91bd-4c0c-9546-93b5c13d7282",
					"diagramNodeId": "f2ba8116-c276-45b7-9e39-e77c646cb57a",
					"simStepLabel": "Return Stream Mapping Arguments",
					"simStepDescription": "The stream handling logic returns an array of arguments for mapping and codec selection (e.g., `-map 0:0 -c:0 copy`) back to the main export function.",
					"isEdge": 1,
					"sourceCodeMapping": {
						"filePath": "src/renderer/src/hooks/useFfmpegOperations.ts",
						"startLine": "327",
						"endLine": "327",
						"relevantVariables": [
							"getMapStreamsArgs",
							"mapStreamsArgs"
						]
					},
					"inputDataExample": "{\"outFormat\": \"mp4\", \"copyFileStreams\": [{\"path\": \"/path/to/video.mkv\", \"streamIds\": [0, 1]}]}",
					"outputDataExample": "{\"streamArgs\": [\"-map\", \"0:0\", \"-c:0\", \"copy\", \"-map\", \"0:1\", \"-c:1\", \"copy\"]}"
				},
				{
					"simStepId": "62349804-6067-4933-a2ad-46da3411ea51",
					"diagramNodeId": "a3ee4c4d-b606-404f-8dab-26546cb1e6b3",
					"simStepLabel": "Assemble Final FFmpeg Command",
					"simStepDescription": "The `losslessCutSingle` function (called by `cutMultiple`) constructs the final array of FFmpeg arguments. It combines input file paths, stream mappings, and crucially, adds the `-f` flag followed by the user-selected `outFormat` to explicitly set the output container format.",
					"isEdge": 0,
					"sourceCodeMapping": {
						"filePath": "src/renderer/src/hooks/useFfmpegOperations.ts",
						"startLine": "406",
						"endLine": "414",
						"relevantVariables": [
							"ffmpegArgs",
							"outFormat",
							"outPath"
						]
					},
					"inputDataExample": "{\"outFormat\": \"mp4\", \"outPath\": \"/path/to/output/video.mp4\", \"mapStreamsArgs\": [\"-map\", \"0:0\", \"-c:0\", \"copy\"]}",
					"outputDataExample": "{\"ffmpegArgs\": [\"-i\", \"/path/to/video.mkv\", \"-ss\", \"0\", \"-to\", \"10\", \"-map\", \"0:0\", \"-c:0\", \"copy\", \"-f\", \"mp4\", \"-y\", \"/path/to/output/video.mp4\"]}"
				},
				{
					"simStepId": "9fb70c29-2c98-41f5-8e77-631c8007c94e",
					"diagramNodeId": "",
					"simStepLabel": "Execute FFmpeg Remux Operation",
					"simStepDescription": "The complete array of FFmpeg arguments is passed to the `runFfmpegWithProgress` function, which spawns the FFmpeg process. This executes the command, causing FFmpeg to read the source media and write a new file with the streams repackaged into the desired container format.",
					"isEdge": 1,
					"sourceCodeMapping": {
						"filePath": "src/renderer/src/hooks/useFfmpegOperations.ts",
						"startLine": "413",
						"endLine": "413",
						"relevantVariables": [
							"runFfmpegWithProgress",
							"ffmpegArgs"
						]
					},
					"inputDataExample": "{\"ffmpegArgs\": [\"-i\", \"/path/to/video.mkv\", \"-f\", \"mp4\", \"-y\", \"/path/to/output/video.mp4\"]}",
					"outputDataExample": "{\"ffmpegArgs\": [\"-i\", \"/path/to/video.mkv\", \"-f\", \"mp4\", \"-y\", \"/path/to/output/video.mp4\"]}"
				}
			],
			"description": "<ul><li>Change the container format of a media file without re-encoding the underlying streams</li><li>- For example, a user can quickly change a video from MKV to MP4 format for better compatibility with certain devices like iPhones</li><li>- This is a lossless and fast operation as it only repackages the existing data</li><li>- A dropdown menu provides a comprehensive list of supported output formats derived from FFmpeg</li><li>- The application intelligently suggests a default output format based on the input file's streams</li></ul>",
			"simulationNodesAndEdges": {
				"9583d83b-6854-4c32-a832-35a82f71552c": {
